mmary": "Use hätte in the counterfactual result clause", "before": "so hatte ich dich gebissen", "after": "so hätte ich dich gebissen", "data": {"confidence": "high"}, "rationale": "The conditional “wenn deine Stunde da wäre” requires the counterfactual “hätte ... gebissen”; indicative hatte incorrectly makes it a past assertion.", "evidence": [], "priority": 2, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "high", "protocol": "PROOF_PROTOCOL", "run": "proof/P022", "date": "2026-10-25"}}, {"id": "03945e50b5e7", "entryId": "kml", "kind": "fix-text", "stage": "proofreading", "target": {"stemId": "kml.II", "boxId": "kml.II.t.infectum", "exampleId": "kml.II.t.infectum.5", "field": "turoyo"}, "summary": "Restore the prefix of gəmkamannole", "before": "u=waʕd-awo mkamánno-le", "after": "u=waʕd-awo gə-mkamánno-le", "data": {"confidence": "high"}, "rationale": "The supplied corpus reads “u waʕdawo gəmkamannole”. The glossary omits the gə- prefix of this verb rather than merely changing the clitic boundary or stress.", "evidence": [{"textId": "R029", "v": 118, "cite": "29/118"}], "priority": 2, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "high", "protocol": "PROOF_PROTOCOL", "run": "proof/P022", "date": "2026-10-25"}}, {"id": "f44104fedf3d", "entryId": "kml", "kind": "fix-text", "stage": "proofreading", "target": {"stemId": "kml.I", "boxId": "kml.I.t.preterit-intransitive", "exampleId": "kml.I.t.preterit-intransitive.4", "field": "translation"}, "summary": "Correct the German noun Tage", "before": "drei ṭage", "after": "drei Tage", "data": {"confidence": "high"}, "rationale": "The German noun is Tage; ṭ is a transcription character accidentally used in the translation. The supplied edition has “Als drei Tage um waren”.", "evidence": [{"textId": "R024", "v": 96, "cite": "24/96"}], "priority": 3, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "high", "protocol": "PROOF_PROTOCOL", "run": "proof/P022", "date": "2026-10-25"}}, {"id": "c36972ad6489", "entryId": "kml", "k